  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Slightly above normal temperatures Thursday with \nrising humidity levels.\n\nSurface high pressure draped from the Ohio Valley to New England \nwill settle southeastward through the first half of Thursday. As \nsuch, warmer air and higher humidity levels will advect into the \nregion, allowing highs Thursday to top out in the mid to upper 80s \nacross the lower elevations and the lower to mid 80s across the \nhigher terrain, with dewpoints climbing into the upper 60s to low \n70s. As such, it will feel rather warm and muggy with heat indices \napproaching the upper 80s across the higher terrain and low 90s in \nthe lower elevations.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Showers and thunderstorms expected Thursday \nafternoon through Friday, where a few thunderstorms may become \nsevere (Marginal Risk for Severe Thunderstorms and Excessive \nRainfall Thursday).\n\nA mid-level trough and attendant weak cold front will drop southeast \ninto the central Great Lakes Thursday afternoon, with weak forcing \nand deeper moisture (PWAT values climbing up towards 1.5 to 1.75 \ninches) overspreading the region out ahead of these features. \nCoupled with the development of modest diurnal instability...this \nwill likely allow for at least some scattered showers and storms to \ndevelop Thursday afternoon...primarily along developing lake breeze \nboundaries to the lee of Lake Erie and also south/east of Lake \nOntario. While a few storms could become strong to marginally severe \nand capable of producing damaging wind gusts and/or locally heavy \nrainfall...this potential may be limited by overall modest \ninstability and poor lapse rates. This said...a Marginal Risk for \nboth Severe Thunderstorms and Excessive Rainfall remains in place \nfor all areas north of the Southern Tier during Thursday.\n\nThe better chance for widespread showers and a few embedded \nthunderstorms will be Thursday night through Friday morning as the \nweak cold front gradually slides southeast across the region. A few \nshowers and scattered storms may linger into Friday afternoon before \nthe front pushes further south of the area.",
